[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have been experimenting with formalizing basic properties of Parse Trees using <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Computability/ContextFreeGrammar.html#ContextFreeGrammar\">Mathlib/Computability/ContextFreeGrammar</a> in <a href=\"https://github.com/shaazib-tanvir/ContextFree/blob/main/ContextFree/ParseTree.lean\">my own repository</a>. So, I wasa wondering how cslib plans to handle CFGs and Parsing Theory?<br>\nI saw a related post in the zulip <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"513188\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/513188-CSLib/topic/Context.20Free.20Grammar.20Results/with/566388157\">#CSLib &gt; Context Free Grammar Results</a> but it seems to have no replies so far.</p>",
        "id": 580713794,
        "sender_full_name": "Syed Shaazib Tanvir",
        "timestamp": 1774027693
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FYI leftmost derivations have been formalized also in this BSc thesis:<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.dmg.tuwien.ac.at/hetzl/teaching/b_leichtfried.pdf\">https://www.dmg.tuwien.ac.at/hetzl/teaching/b_leichtfried.pdf</a><br>\n<span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"759645\">@Tobias Leichtfried</span></p>",
        "id": 581382809,
        "sender_full_name": "Martin Dvořák",
        "timestamp": 1774361853
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the information.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In this proof we see the need for DerivesLeftmostIn as otherwise strong induction would not be pos-<br>\nsible.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I actually ran into the same problem of not being able to do strong induction on the size of Mathlib's <code>Derives</code> type because of proof irrelevance and had to make an identical non-Prop type and prove its equivalence with <code>Derives</code> (it seems like this paper's solution of adding another inductive proposition about an n-step derivation is  a lot cleaner)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Derives'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContextFreeGrammar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">NT</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">NT</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">refl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">NT</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Derives'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trans</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Symbol</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">NT</span><span class=\"o\">)}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h_produces</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Produces</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">derives</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Derives'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Derives'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I wonder what the advantages of an inductively defined Prop are over Type for  things like derivations, reductions etc.</p>",
